From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] local: serial: qcom-geni: rebalance the IRQ when a forced
 suspend or resume fails

7.3 carries upstream d0cd9c8d0fd5 ("serial: qcom-geni: add force
suspend/resume to system sleep callbacks"). 1006 masks a non-console port's
IRQ in qcom_geni_serial_suspend() and unmasks it in resume, and upstream's
error paths know nothing of that mask:

  - pm_runtime_force_suspend() failing returns the error with the port
    suspended and its IRQ masked. The PM core does not call resume for the
    device whose suspend failed, so nothing ever unmasks it.
  - pm_runtime_force_resume() failing returns before the enable_irq() that
    balances the suspend.

Either way the port stays deaf. On the AYN Odin 3 that port is the gamepad
MCU's (rsinput, 89c000.serial): built-in controls dead until reboot.

armada (packages/kernel/patches/0534 at d2bcf6fd3343) backported the
upstream commit to 7.2 with exactly this handling folded in; this is that
handling alone, on 7.3's version of the code.

---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -2129,7 +2129,12 @@
 	if (!console_suspend_enabled && uart_console(uport))
 		return 0;
 
-	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	if (ret && !uart_console(uport)) {
+		uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
+		enable_irq(uport->irq);
+	}
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
@@ -2141,8 +2146,11 @@
 
 	if (console_suspend_enabled || !uart_console(uport)) {
 		ret = pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret) {
+			if (!uart_console(uport))
+				enable_irq(uport->irq);
 			return ret;
+		}
 	}
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
